  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Patchy fog and low clouds overnight through early \nthis morning.\n\nThe last of the showers and thunderstorms ahead of an incoming cold \nfront early this morning, will continue to progress east towards the \neastern Lake Ontario region. In its wake, lingering moisture is \nsupporting low stratus and fog to develop across western New York. \nThe low stratus and fog wil continue to develop across the Niagara \nFrontier and western Southern Tier well into the morning hours \nbefore dissipating within a few hours past sunrise today.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Trending warmer this weekend and into next week.\n\nMid to upper level ridge will build across the Great Lakes this \nweekend before shifting east into the Northeastern portions of the \nCONUS throughout the course of next week. Temperatures will \ngradually increase by the end of the weekend and into early next \nweek. Heat and humidity will then increase further throughout the \nmiddle and end of next week, which may result in the potential for \nheat-related headlines as the risk for dangerous heat indices \nincrease. However, due to the potential for scattered showers and \nthunderstorms both Tuesday and Wednesday there may be some short-\nterm relief from the heat. Stay tuned!",
